# Phase 3 changed this gate: the secret scanner's configuration now accepts at most SIX allowlist blocks (five in Phase 3, the sixth added in Phase 4 for the JWT dial test) (the fourth and fifth are the two decided exceptions of Phase 3: a selftest fixture and a test assertion, both in published history). The fault appends a sixth, narrow-looking block (one rule, one commit, no regex), which is exactly the quiet drift the limit exists to stop; the gate must name the count and the limit. The control is the real configuration, which must be green.
GATE=gitleaks-config
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=check-gitleaks-config on the real repository
CMD=bash scripts/check-gitleaks-config.sh
MESSAGE=8 [[allowlists]] blocks (at most 7 are accepted
MESSAGE=check-gitleaks-config: RED
